The bug was caused by incorrect memory management when handling the host string for IPv6 addresses. The original code allocated memory for the `host` pointer but did not properly manage the memory, leading to potential memory leaks or incorrect deallocation. This was particularly problematic when the function attempted to free the memory, as it was freeing the wrong pointer, which could lead to undefined behavior when parsing IPv6 addresses.



